    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Heap / top-k</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Quickselect</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/k-closest-points-to-origin/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 973</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>K Closest Points to Origin</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">You need the k smallest distances, not a sorted list. Keep a max-heap of size k whose root is the worst point kept; a new point only has to beat the root. O(n log k) time, O(k) space, and it works on a stream. Quickselect gets O(n) on average when all points are in memory. Compare squared distances: no square roots.</p>\n"
  },
